WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.029
Challenging weather is any condition or combination of conditions that reduces control,

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:08.725
visibility, endurance, sensor performance, data quality, or recovery margin.

00:00:08.725 --> 00:00:13.654
It is defined by the aircraft, crew, mission, site, and current rules,

00:00:13.654 --> 00:00:16.529
not by how dramatic the weather appears.

00:00:16.529 --> 00:00:21.457
Wind and gusts can displace a small aircraft and increase power use.

00:00:21.457 --> 00:00:26.797
Rain, snow, fog, humidity, dust, or smoke can reduce visibility and contaminate sensors.

00:00:26.797 --> 00:00:30.493
Heat and cold affect batteries, electronics, crews, and payloads.

00:00:30.493 --> 00:00:31.315
Conditions compound.

00:00:31.315 --> 00:00:36.654
Moderate wind may be manageable with a warm battery and clear recovery area,

00:00:36.654 --> 00:00:41.993
yet become unacceptable when cold, haze, difficult terrain, and weak signal occur together.

00:00:41.993 --> 00:00:44.868
Risk assessment must consider the whole system.

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:47.333
Rapid change is itself a hazard.

00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:53.083
A mission may launch in acceptable conditions and encounter a passing shower, gust front,

00:00:53.083 --> 00:00:55.136
forming fog, falling temperature, smoke,

00:00:55.136 --> 00:00:58.011
or deteriorating visibility before collection is complete.

00:00:58.011 --> 00:01:00.065
Weather also determines mission value.

00:01:00.065 --> 00:01:02.529
Unstable footage, obscured lenses, deep haze,

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:07.458
or poor contrast may produce data that cannot support the intended decision.

00:01:07.458 --> 00:01:11.976
Completing the route is not success when the evidence is unusable.

00:01:11.976 --> 00:01:14.851
Conservative decision-making and legal compliance come first.

00:01:14.851 --> 00:01:18.958
Follow current official information and manufacturer limitations, preserve generous margins,

00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:21.011
and delay, modify, return, land,

00:01:21.011 --> 00:01:25.940
or cancel rather than force an aircraft or crew beyond safe capability.
